      "answer": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{22}{5}}$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Taking a general point $P$ of $ON$ to have position vector $\\lambda(3\\mathbf j+\\mathbf k)$, form an equation in $\\lambda$ by equating $\\overrightarrow{ON}\\cdot\\overrightarrow{MP}=0$, applying Pythagoras to triangle $OMP$, or equating the derivative of $MP$ to zero. [M1] Printed scalar product: $(-2,-2+3\\lambda,\\lambda)\\cdot(0,3,1)=0$.\nSolve and obtain $\\lambda=3/5$. [A1]\nSubstitute for $\\lambda$ and calculate $MP$. [M1] Guidance: $\\overrightarrow{MP}=-2\\mathbf i-(1/5)\\mathbf j+(3/5)\\mathbf k$.\nObtain $\\sqrt{22/5}$. [A1 AG]\nAlternative method: use a scalar product to find the projection $OQ$ of $OM$ on $ON$ [M1]; obtain $OQ=6/\\sqrt{10}$ [A1]; use Pythagoras in triangle $OMQ$ to find $MQ$ [M1]; obtain $\\sqrt{22/5}$ [A1 AG]. Total: 4.",
